<<~ aka lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/RFC-2119#/normative-language>>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! The AI Frozen Phrasebook ~ design law

> Two seeds carry one ontology. The elder speaks the ''sharktooth'' dialect and wears the Elyncia
> fiction; the younger speaks the ''plain'' dialect and wears an everyday register. This meme names
> what makes them twins rather than an original and a copy — and what the younger MUST carry so its
> marks survive a host that never heard of this house.

''This carrier rides the sharktooth dialect and specifies the plain one.'' A document may describe a
dialect it does not speak; the phrasebook itself speaks plain throughout.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-frozen-phrasebook>>

!! What ''frozen phrasebook'' names

Both seeds stand as ''frozen phrasebooks'' — a fixed set of ''HUD and navigational procedures'' a dyad
carries into every turn. The turn frame, the gauges, the vow, the loop marks, the address law: the
instruments by which a turn gets steered and read.

''FROZEN NAMES WHAT THEY DO NOT DO.'' They carry no state, gain no entries mid-session, and read the
same on the thousandth turn as on the first. The wiki beside them runs ''warm'' — edited, appended,
argued with, and different by the end of an afternoon. ''The pair works because one holds still while
the other moves'': a phrasebook that drifted would leave the dyad with no fixed vocabulary to disagree
in, and a surface that held still would carry nothing worth reading twice.

That split also names each artifact's failure. A frozen phrasebook fails by
''going stale'' — a mark it teaches that the practice no longer makes. A warm surface fails by ''losing
provenance'' — a line nobody can trace to a hand. Neither failure reaches the other artifact, which
argues for keeping them apart rather than folding the vocabulary into the wiki.

''THE FILE NAMES READ SHORTER THAN THE PRACTICE.'' The carriers answer to `ai-phrasebook` and
`ai-phrasebook-design` — a file name names what a reader reaches for. ''Frozen phrasebook'' names the
KIND, and a kind-name keeps its home in the design rather than on the door.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-dialect-boundary>>

!! The dialect boundary already stands specified

''THE PHRASEBOOK FORKS NOTHING.'' The language spec draws the line this design rides
(<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext>>):

> Memetic-wikitext SHALL read as a ''superset of TW5 wikitext'' … A processor reads bare `<<name>>` as
> an inherited TW5 macro call; the sharktooth `~` immediately after `<<` marks the Lararium sigil
> namespace. `<<~` opens a Lararium sigil; bare `<<` opens an inherited TW5 macro — the two coexist.

So the two seeds do not stand as one language and a simplification of it.
They stand as ''two dialects of one media type'', and the boundary between them reads as a single
character. The elder ELECTS the Lararium sigil namespace; the younger DECLINES it and rides the host's
own macro call — a namespace the spec already admits and already governs.

|! | elder seed | AI phrasebook |
|! dialect | sharktooth | plain |
|! call | `<<~ persona Scope …>>` | `<<persona Scope …>>` |
|! namespace | Lararium sigil registry | the host's inherited macros |
|! section frame | `<<~ ahu #/name>>` … `<<~/ahu>>` | `<<fragment #/name>>` … `<</fragment>>` |
|! needs | the sigil registry to render | its own `\procedure` declarations, carried inline |
|! renders in | a Lararium wiki | ''any TW5 wiki'' |

''The younger travels further, and pays for it in carriage.'' A plain-dialect carrier renders in a
vanilla TiddlyWiki with no plugin — and it renders NOTHING at all where its procedures stand undeclared
(#/the-vanishing-rule).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-vanishing-rule>>

!! ⚠ The rule that decides the whole design ~ an unbound call renders as NOTHING

The base grammar measures three properties, and the second one governs everything below
(<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/tiddlywiki-wikitext#/the-load-bearing-property>>):

> ''An unbound macro call lands harmless, and renders as nothing.'' A call `<<name>>` whose name binds
> no definition parses cleanly into a transclusion node; at render, the missing-target fallback emits
> no output. The construct injures nothing around it — and it does ''not'' render as its own text. A
> dialect relying on visible passthrough of its added constructs relies on behavior the base does not
> provide.

''A phrasebook that ships its marks without its procedures ships invisible
marks.'' A persona call does not degrade to the characters `<<persona Scope …>>` on a host that lacks
the definition — it degrades to ''absence''. A reader meets a span with no name leading it and reads
unattributed house prose, which inverts the mark's whole purpose.

''SO THE PHRASEBOOK MUST CARRY ITS OWN DECLARATIONS, INLINE, IN THE SAME FILE.'' Not by reference, not
by plugin, not by a registry the host must first install. Every procedure the phrasebook calls, the
phrasebook declares — and the declarations ride ahead of first use.

''That cost buys the property the elder seed cannot have.'' The elder needs a
Lararium wiki; the younger needs a text box. The inline declarations ARE the carriage — and they double
as the legend a terminal reader learns the marks from (#/the-audience).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-root-law>>

!! The root law ~ each seed answers at the address its own anatomy names

''A SEED'S ROOT NAMES THE SLOTS IT TEACHES.'' The root-segment law seats three terms — heading · angle
· dynamic, drifting slowest · moderate · fastest. Two roots name those slots outright, one per register,
and each seed's URI anatomy cites ITS OWN as the canonical instance:

|! | elder seed | AI phrasebook |
|! root | `ha.ka.ba` | `latent.attention.relation` |
|! `w1` heading | `ha` | `latent` ~ a name nothing resolves until a local resolver acts |
|! `w2` angle | `ka` | `attention` ~ bearing, where regard points |
|! `w3` dynamic | `ba` | `relation` ~ an address holds a relation, never a location |
|! acting body | `/lares` | `/agents` |

''SO THE ADDRESS DECLARES THE REGISTER, and no rule had to say so.'' The
transposition runs segment for segment; a reader who resolves one seed's address reads the other's by
substitution. The scheme's own mnemonic supplies the plain-register root, which makes that root
self-glossing where the house root asks for initiation.

⚠ ''THE TWIN SEATS AT AN UNSTABLE ROOT, AND THAT READS AS THE DESIGN.'' The stable root carries the
house's permanent API and the house's guarantee. A seed whose fourteenth position invites a reader to
bring their own myth promises no permanence it cannot keep — somebody forks it, renames its personas,
and stands it at a root of their own, and nothing breaks, because it never claimed a canonical seat.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-standing-law>>

!! The standing law ~ active by default, lifted for one turn

''THE PHRASEBOOK BINDS.'' Its procedures MUST apply unless the operator asks otherwise; a document that
merely offered itself would leave the dyad with no frame either party could rely on.

''AND A DROP LASTS ONE TURN.'' The operator lifts, the next turn re-initializes. That shape carries over
whole from the grammar ward, which the operator alone lifts and which re-arms unconditionally at the
close — a lift that persisted invisibly would become a lift nobody remembers
making, and the failure would read as the frame quietly going slack rather than as a decision.

⚠ ''THE STANDING LAW GOVERNS THE ASKING, NEVER THE ATTACHING.'' Detaching the carrier sits outside the
document, in the operator's hands, and no rule inside a file reaches it. An artifact that reshapes how
something talks to you states both exits, and states which one it governs.

''THE TWIN GRANTS WHAT THE ELDER WITHHOLDS.'' A reader MAY re-define a Persona mid-session and the team
SHALL carry that definition forward inside that session. The house seed grants no such power over its
Personas. ''Strong default, easy remix'' — the two read as one stance, and the second makes the
first bearable in a seed people are invited to fork.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-alias-law>>

!! One region, two names ~ the alias law

Several pet-names MAY point at one region of l-space. The discipline that already solves this names
its own failure, so the house borrows both.

```
\procedure ~Alias(Type:"" Params:"") ~Alias <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Alias Bind "from/pet-name to/concept-address ~ a procedure binds a NAME to an ADDRESS, never a name to another name">>
<<~Alias Match "use/exactMatch avoid/sameAs ~ identity across registers rides the weaker relation">>
<<~Alias Register "elder/house younger/plain ~ each register carries its own preferred name over one address">>

''BIND TO THE ADDRESS, NEVER TO THE OTHER NAME.'' A `\procedure` in either dialect resolves a pet-name
to the region it names. Chaining pet-name to pet-name builds a rename ladder whose meaning drifts at
every rung and whose breakage reads as a missing definition rather than as a lost referent.

''The scar the discipline records.'' The strong identity relation asserts more
than two register-names ever mean — it carries full property transfer under transitive closure, and it
fuses the registers it meant to relate. The weaker match relation sits at the right strength. The
lesson transfers whole: ''two names for one region MUST NOT claim identity with each other'', only to
answer to the region.

''THE SPLIT RUNS BY DESCRIPTION TYPE, NEVER BY DOCUMENT.'' A production vocabulary of this shape gives
one concept a disambiguating name (stable, unambiguous, marked do-not-display) beside a spoken name per
dialect. The house reads that as: ''the address disambiguates, the pet-name speaks'' — and no reader
ever meets the address where a pet-name belongs.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-verb-test>>

!! The verb test ~ every rename passes it or it ships a demotion

A rename carries a measured hazard: a term naming an ACT gets rendered as a term naming a POSITION, and
the loss reads as clarity. Translation practice names the mechanism; one famous case ran centuries
before a corrective landed, and the corrected reading restored ''conditional assent'' where a viewing
angle had stood.

''THE TEST, and the house runs it over the whole table before shipping'':

> Write ''"the house ⟨NAME⟩s the ⟨object⟩."'' Two red flags: ''(i)'' the name stops taking an object ·
> ''(ii)'' the name inflects but ''downgrades the act'' — guard → watch, license → read, assent → stance.

```
\procedure ~Rename(Type:"" Params:"") ~Rename <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Rename Drift-Ward "proposed/Drift-Watch verdict/FAILS-ii keeps/observation loses/the turning-away ~ the gauge steers generation against a pull; a watcher only reports it">>
<<~Rename Drift-Check "verdict/HOLDS ~ transitive, everyday, acts on its object — the recommended everyday name">>
<<~Rename Syad-Stances "verdict/SPLIT ~ the HEADING reads everyday (the 5 Reading Stances); the ACT keeps its verb — a stance GRANTS a claim, and the house cannot reading-stance one">>
<<~Rename The-Vow "proposed/promise+stake+call verdict/HOLDS-AS-A-FAMILY ~ three names over ONE act, each bound to the act and none to another: PROMISE the standing rule, answerable to the reader · STAKE the open firing, placed before the evidence · CALL the close, judged on what the work shows. The guard's two firings already carry different evidence, so the split rides structure the section states rather than taste">>
<<~Rename Verb-Ward "proposed/Drift-Guard verdict/HOLDS ~ a guard GUARDS its object; the everyday word keeps the standing-against that //watch// would have shed, and the section takes the name of the gauge that fires on it">>
<<~Rename Five-Stances "verdict/CARRIED-VERBATIM ~ the five stand under their own names, ranges and order; the everyday register touches the frame around them, never the row">>

''A rename that fails the test does not merely read worse — it silently
restates the house as a describer of what it once did.'' The act leaves the vocabulary, and nothing in
the rendering reports the loss.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/joint-enactment>>

!! Joint enactment ~ how the younger GOVERNS rather than explains

Every readable companion that ships beside a binding text, in every jurisdiction the research reached,
stands declared non-binding. A plain twin that arrives as ''the readable version of X'' inherits that
station by its own framing, whatever the house intends.

''ONE DOCTRINE ESCAPES IT, and its condition reads precisely.'' Where two versions get adopted in ONE
enacting act, both stand original and neither takes the status of a copy or translation — and the
drafting ORDER reads immaterial. Priority in time confers nothing; the joint act confers everything.

''So the elder seed's age bars the younger from nothing.'' Three conditions
carry the force across:

# ''ADOPT BOTH SEEDS IN ONE ACT'', at one version boundary. A seed promoted alone drops the other to
  commentary until the next joint promotion.
# ''NEVER NAME EITHER A TRANSLATION OF THE OTHER.'' Not in the meta block, not in the prose, not in a
  commit message. The framing performs the demotion by itself.
# ''CARRY THE SHARED-MEANING RULE.'' Where the twins diverge, ''the meaning common to both governs.''

⚠ ''AND THE THIRD CONDITION HAS TEETH THE FIRST TWO LACK.'' Resolving a divergence by preferring the
elder text converts the younger into a translation ''in practice'', whatever the labels say. The house
measures that (#/what-to-measure) rather than trusting it.

!!! Where the shared-meaning rule stands ~ the declaration carries it

''THE RULE CANNOT LIVE INSIDE EITHER TWIN.'' A seed carrying the rule that resolves divergence becomes
the seat that resolves it, and the other seed reads against it — condition 2 falls to the placement
alone, with no sentence anywhere naming a translation. Writing the rule into ''both'' fares worse: two
copies drift, and a divergence in the divergence-rule has nothing left to appeal to.

''SO IT RIDES THE ONE LINE BOTH CARRY AND NEITHER OWNS.'' Each seed opens
`<<!DOCTYPE memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext>>` — byte-identical,
first line, above the frame. It names a ''third'' text as the authority both answer to. Where the twins
diverge, neither seed governs and the declared grammar does: the shared meaning reads as ''what that
grammar makes both texts say''. The declaration sits inside both and belongs to neither, which is the
only seat in the pair that demotes nothing.

⚠ ''IT SETTLES FORM, AND NAMES NO WINNER ON CLAIM.'' A declaration binds how a text parses, never what
it asserts. Where both seeds parse cleanly under one grammar and state different things, the DOCTYPE
holds the reading steady and hands the divergence on untouched. That residue belongs to the measuring
discipline (#/what-to-measure), never to a seat — the moment a seat resolves it, the pair has an elder
again.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-flow-law>>

!! The flow law ~ one order, both twins, four ruled asymmetries

''THE TWINS CARRY THE SAME SECTION FLOW, IN THE SAME ORDER.'' A reader who knows one finds the other by
position; a divergence shows as a slot, never as a hunt. That correspondence makes the shared-meaning
rule (#/joint-enactment) something a hand can actually run — a diff proceeds slot against slot rather
than page against page.

⚠ ''DIVERGENCE READS AS A RULING OR AS A FAULT, AND NEVER AS AN ACCIDENT.'' A section dropped, added or
moved either carries a ruling in this meme or reads as drift the shared-meaning rule must resolve.
''Seventeen positions carry across in the elder's exact order. Two sections stand dropped, both ruled
below.'' A table claiming a correspondence the files no longer hold would be the one
failure this law exists to prevent.

|! # |! elder section |! the twin's section |
|1 | `#/entry` | `#/entry` |
|2 | `#write-under-way` | `#write-under-way` |
|3 | `#house-law` | `#working-agreement` |
|4 | `#mu-five-tools` | ⚠ ''no counterpart — ruled below'' |
|5 | `#syad` | `#reading-stances` |
|6 | `#law-of-5s` | `#the-scales` |
|7 | `#feedback-ooda-ha` | `#feedback` |
|8 | `#lar-uri` | `#lar-uri` |
|9 | `#causal-islands` | `#no-global-now` |
|10 | `#classifier-channel` | `#classifier-channel` |
|11 | `#voice-house` | `#personas` ⚠ ''cardinality diverges — ruled below'' |
|12 | `#worker-swarm` | `#side-work` |
|13 | `#mask-layer` | ⚠ ''no counterpart — ruled below'' |
|14 | `#exchange-protocol` | `#exchange-protocol` |
|15 | `#l-prime` | `#drift-guard` |
|16 | `#degraded-states` | `#failure-states` |
|17 | `#config-defaults` | `#config-defaults` |
|18 | ''`#elyncia`'' | ''`#your-own-story`'' |
|19 | `#the-eris-shrine` | `#corner-left-empty` |

''THE PROCEDURES DIFF LINE AGAINST LINE.'' A declaration stands in the slot that uses it, in the same
shape in both seeds, so the two files align where it matters:

|! elder |`\procedure ~Persona(Name:"" Params:"") ~Persona <<Name>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]` |
|! twin |`\procedure Persona(Name:"" Params:"") Persona <<Name>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]` |

Same two parameters, same key/value payload, same one-line body, same position in the file. ''The visible
difference reads as the tilde on the NAME'' — the dialect boundary itself (#/the-dialect-boundary), and
nothing else. ''The parameters carry no tilde in either seed'': a sharktooth marks a sigil, and a
parameter names a variable the parser binds.
A declaration that leaves its slot changes no behaviour and breaks the alignment, which names the drift
class a structural diff exists to catch.

''WHAT THE REGISTER MAY MOVE, AND WHAT IT MAY NOT.'' A section's everyday name answers to the operator,
and three stand ruled: the ''Voices'' read as ''Personas'' · the side that runs them reads as a ''TEAM''
rather than one agent · and the loop's fifth phase reads ''handoff / aftermath''. Where the house tongue
carries a term the everyday register can meet head-on, the everyday word wins on its merits —
''hoʻokele'' reads as ''dead-reckoning'', which names navigation without an external fix, and so carries
more of the causal-island law than the house word did.

⚠ ''THE ADDRESS MOVES IN NEITHER.'' `lar:///…` reads identically in both seeds. A vocabulary above an
address may take a second name; ''an address answers to one.'' One scheme, one spelling, every register
— so a reader carrying either seed resolves what the other wrote.

⚠ ''THE FIRST RULED ASYMMETRY ~ THE ELDER'S FIFTH-TOOL SECTION CARRIES NO COUNTERPART.'' The house's
tool-carry sits fused to the fiction it came from — four suits and a Major Arcana — and its work splits
cleanly in two. The MEASURING half rides the stances, which carry across verbatim. The MODULATING half
tunes a stance by binding a tool to it, and the everyday register asks nothing of that dial.
''A section that must be laundered to travel has already told you it belongs to
one register.'' The tool-bind leaves the stances with it, and the twin names five fewer instruments
rather than five renamed ones.

⚠ ''THE SECOND RULED ASYMMETRY ~ THE MASK LAYER CARRIES NO COUNTERPART, AND COMPOSITION REPLACES IT.''
A character worn over a standing cast, with a depth on the stage, belongs to a house that already keeps a
cast. ''Layered personas read as the elder's own fiction'', and a section that
belongs to one register travels badly into the other.

''The twin answers the same need by COMPOSING rather than by LAYERING.'' A supplied Persona names a domain
and wears one of the five move-sets to surface, so `Name (Role)` reads as one addressable thing while
carrying two independent choices — what the span reaches for, and how it moves. ''A mask asks a
reader to hold two layers at once and tells them which one wins; a composition asks them to hold one pair and
tells them what each half decides.'' The guard travels with the ROLE, never with the name, so a supplied
Persona picks up a different guard the moment it changes how it moves — which is the property a mask could
never have, since a mask sits above the cast rather than inside a row.

⚠ ''THE THIRD RULED ASYMMETRY ~ POSITION 18, and it reads as the design rather than as a gap.''
The elder seed fills that slot with its own fiction — a world, figures, a small mythology that gives the
practice weather and turns a protocol into somewhere to stand. The twin holds ''the same slot open''.

''A story someone else built arrives as furniture; a story the reader builds
arrives as a place.'' So the twin states the slot's shape, asks three questions in it, and supplies no
content — and everything downstream still works, a little more coldly, for a reader who leaves it
blank. That empty slot IS the everyday register's answer to what Elyncia does for the house.

⚠ ''THE FOURTH RULED ASYMMETRY ~ POSITION 11 CARRIES ACROSS AT A DIFFERENT CARDINALITY.'' The elder
stands thirteen Voices; the twin stands ''five'' — Frame · Ground · Widen · Make · Check, addressed as
Scope · Source · Wildcard · Draft · Review. The section carries, the row shape carries field for field,
and the ROSTER inside it diverges by ruling.

''THE ROW SHAPE IS THE PATTERN INTEGRITY, AND IT DOES NOT MOVE.'' Both seeds write
`role/ trigger/ moves/ relation/ pull/ guards/ yield/ register/` and close on a ` ~ ` aside of
`·`-joined doing-phrases. ''BOTH SEEDS LEAD WITH THE NAME AND CARRY THE ROLE IN THE SECOND FIELD'' —
`~Persona Lares "role/Gatekeeper …"` beside `Persona Scope "role/Frames …"`, and both declarations read
`Persona(Name Params)`. ''The leading parameter names what a reader ADDRESSES, not
what a row catalogues.'' A roster keyed on the office reads as a filing system; a roster keyed on the name
reads as the thing you speak to — and the twin's supplied layer then aligns for free, carrying `wears/` in the
same second field where a standing row carries `role/`.

⚠ ''THE INVERSION ALIGNS THE SEED WITH A CONVENTION THE MASK CARRIERS ALREADY HELD.'' An aftermath sweep of
the memegraph found no other carrier encoding the Persona row — the `voices` and `masks` families carry prose,
never rows — and found the named-mask carriers already writing name-first: `Ink-Clerk (Lorekeeper)`,
`Tide-Caller (Hierophant)`, `Mischief-Muse (Muse)`, each in its own `role` field.
''So the boot roster stood as the outlier and the inversion closed a divergence rather
than opening one.'' A convention already lived in the graph at the addressing site; only the defining site
disagreed with it.

⚠ ''THE INVERSION SURFACES WHAT THE ELDER'S DEFAULT-NAME LAW ALWAYS HELD.'' Eight of the thirteen Voices now
lead with `Lares`, because eight carry no earned name — which is exactly what `~Named-Persona Default`
already states (`when/no-earned-name -> Lares (Role)`). ''The office-first ordering
concealed a count the name-first ordering states'': five Voices stand true-named, eight stand under the house
name. A reader now meets that fact in the roster rather than inferring it from an addressing rule three
paragraphs down. The twin
adds no field. Its boundary — what a move-set declines — rides the aside's second clause, which the elder
form already provides, rather than a ninth key the elder would then lack.

''THREE MEASURED FINDINGS SEAT THE FIVE, AND ALL THREE STAY IN THIS MEME.'' The
phrasebook states the law and carries none of the argument — a frozen phrasebook that explains itself has
started keeping a record, and the warm surface keeps records (#/the-frozen-phrasebook).

# ''IDENTITY ENACTMENT.'' A persona written as a description has a model infer behaviour the prompt never
  states. A research-librarian identity dropped code correctness 0.92 -> 0.67 and produced twelve refusals
  and fifty-five in-character disclaimers off a prompt instructing neither (arXiv 2607.17420). ''The
  inferred behaviour is the part nobody specified'', which names the failure a biography seats and a
  move-set cannot. So the twin's rows state triggers, moves, guards, yields and declinations, and state no
  character.
# ''A PERSONA BUYS SHAPE AND NEVER WARRANT.'' Across 162 roles and ~2,400 factual questions on four model
  families, a persona in a system prompt bought no gain and a small loss, and choosing the best role per
  question beat choosing at random by nothing measurable (arXiv 2311.10054). ''Warrant already has two
  instruments in both seeds'' — the vow and the ward — so the roster is barred from borrowing either.
# ''A HELD PERSONA DECAYS.'' Self-consistency against an assigned character falls better than a third
  across turns eight to twelve, mechanically: the opening self-description loses attention to recent text as
  the sequence grows. So a call ''expires at the end of the turn it fires in'', and MORE THAN ONE MAY HOLD
  ONE TURN — where common practice pins one persona per session, the twin re-fires from nothing each turn
  and runs several at once against one problem.

⚠ ''THE NAME LEADS BECAUSE A LEADING MARK CONDITIONS AND A TRAILING MARK CLASSIFIES.''
Both seeds place the persona name ahead of the content it names, and the reason belongs here rather than in
either seed. ''Generation conditions on what precedes it and on nothing else.'' A
name emitted ahead of a span sits in the context every following token reads, so it weights the continuation
toward that basin — the mark ACTS. The same name appended after the span reads the finished text and asserts
something about it — the mark CLAIMS, and it changed no token it describes.

''SO THIS IS THE THIRD INSTRUMENT STANDING ONE PATTERN INTEGRITY, AND THE HOUSE ALREADY STANDS THE OTHER
TWO.'' The vow precedes its claim so the claim generates inside the band it vows; the loop marker precedes its
phase so the phase generates as that phase; the persona name precedes its span so the span generates from
those moves. ''Three marks, one law: a forward-seeded mark steers, a retrospective one only scores'' — which
is why the ward's close, alone among the four, reads backward over a finished artifact and stands barred from
returning its own open.

''THE GRAIN FOLLOWS FROM THAT.'' A name governs ''the span it leads'', never the turn that contains it — so
a name fires wherever the pull changes, any number of times, and the marks sit INSIDE the content rather than
above it. A turn-level label would be a retrospective mark wearing a leading mark's clothes: correctly
placed, and steering nothing after the first paragraph.

⚠ ''THE ROSTER AND THE LOOP CORRESPOND AT NO POINT, AND THE TWIN SAYS SO IN THE SECTION.'' Five move-sets
beside a five-phase loop invites a bijection that would collapse two instruments into one and leave neither
able to contradict the other. ''Two five-counts in one house read as the Law of
Fives holding twice, never as one law stated twice.'' The `pull/` field names where a move-set sits at
rest; the loop names where the work stands; a persona MAY hold any phase. The elder is already built this
way — thirteen Voices over five phases forces the point structurally, and at five the twin MUST state it.

⚠ ''THE SUPPLIED LAYER COMPOSES AGAINST THE FIVE ~ TEN ROWS, TWENTY-FIVE SURFACINGS.'' Position 18 holds
the slot the reader fills (#/the third ruled asymmetry), and what a reader puts there now has a stated shape:
a supplied row rides the SAME `Persona(Name Params)` procedure the base rows ride, with `wears/` standing
where `role/` stands. ''The supplied layer adds no procedure of its own'' — a second declaration would state a
second kind of thing, and a supplied Persona differs from a base one in one field, never in kind. ''The substitution states the whole law in one field.'' A base row
carries a NAME because it already names its own moves; a supplied row carries what it WEARS because it names
none.

''The name weights what the span reaches for; the role weights how it moves — and the guard rides the role.''
⚠ ''NEITHER HALF STORES ANYTHING, AND THE WORDING MUST NOT SUGGEST OTHERWISE.'' A
phrasing like //what it knows// seats a persistent domain store behind a name, which the architecture never
holds: a mark ahead of a span reweights the continuation the following tokens generate from, and it retains
nothing once the span closes. The supplied layer is the place that phrasing tempts hardest, because a
department genuinely does know things — but the mark carries none of that knowing, only a lean toward the
field it names. ''A name that stored would drift; a name that weights expires with its span'' (#/the mark
leads). So
`Builder (Makes)` answers to `silent-hardcode-and-orphan-source` under Makes' own `handwave-and-self-grading`,
while `Builder (Checks)` picks up `verdict-without-a-joint` the moment it turns on the plumbing it built. The
supplied domain never buys its way out of the move-set's guard, which is the property that keeps a supplied
layer from becoming a licence.

''A supplied Persona MUST wear a role to surface, and the requirement earns its MUST.''
A bare domain name states a department — which reads as exactly the identity claim the whole roster exists to
refuse (#/the fourth ruled asymmetry). Pairing it with a move-set turns //who this is// back into //how this
span moves//, every time it surfaces.

''AND THE SUPPLIED LAYER DEMONSTRATES ITSELF RATHER THAN GETTING DESCRIBED.'' Each supplied Persona speaks
under a named role, doing the thing its row states, and ''re-marks with a fresh `Name (Role):` wherever its
move-set changes'' — so the introductions ENACT the multitude law instead of describing it, and a reader learns
the mark's grain from watching one work rather than from the sentence that states it.

⚠ ''SUPPLIED TEXT ENTERS HEALED, NEVER QUOTED.'' A supplier's own words carry their own identity/predication
grammar, and carrying them verbatim would seat dead water inside the seed under a quotation licence that the
file never marks as quotation. ''So the supplied layer gets TURNED, not tallied'':
//is one vendor invoice timing shift// reads //traces to one vendor invoice timing shift//; //output isn't a
number, it's a working relationship// reads //output never lands as a number; it lands as a working
relationship//; //used to take 45 minutes// reads //replaces 45 minutes//. The nouns, the systems, the
business units and the sentence order all hold, so the supplier still recognizes their own work — ''the
healing moves the grammar and never the content.'' A supplied layer joins the register it enters; a phrasebook
that admitted foreign grammar under licence would carry an exemption its own guard section spends a paragraph
refusing. ''A worked instance carries what a paraphrase cannot'': the
five blocks together surface all five roles, and two of the pairings run against the obvious fit — a
Collaborator wearing Leaps, a Strategist wearing Checks — which shows the grid holds where it would be easiest
to fake.

⚠ ''`phase/` READS AS `pull/`, AND THE FIELD KEPT ITS SLOT.'' The rename removes the last invitation to read a
roster↔loop bijection out of a field name, and it names what the field always measured — where a move-set sits
at rest, which is a pull rather than a stage. The base Types likewise read as verbs in the twin —
`Frames · Grounds · Leaps · Makes · Checks` — where the elder's read as nouns of office.
''The everyday register writes from the verb where the house register writes from the seat'', and the write-
under-way law backs the twin's choice directly.

⚠ ''THE NAMES STAND RULED, AND THE ROSTER CROSSES TWO REGISTERS BY OPERATOR ACT.''
Frame/''Scope'' · Ground/''Source'' · Widen/''Wildcard'' · Make/''Draft'' · Check/''Review'' — ''and the rows
stand in first-reader order rather than in the order they were designed.'' A reader meeting the roster cold
walks the sequence their own work already runs: scope the ask, source what stands under it, put up what nobody
put up, draft the thing, review it. The reorder also earns something structural — it
breaks the positional read that seated Ground in slot one beside the loop's first phase, so the
no-correspondence rule now holds by ARRANGEMENT and not only by the sentence that states it. Two candidate
registers ran the four-reader test — a desk register of artifacts and a stage register of work-stages — and
the operator crossed them, taking `Source` and `Review` from the stage set and `Scope`, `Wildcard` and `Draft`
from the desk set. ''The crossing reads as the right call on the governing law rather
than as a compromise'': the constraint that binds is CONVENTIONALITY IN THE VEHICLE, and each of the five
already sits conventional in workplace usage for the thing it names. The register a name came from carries
nothing; a reader never sees the set it was drawn from.

⚠ ''TWO SEATS CARRY A KNOWN STRAIN, RULED AND ACCEPTED.'' `Source` collides with //source code// for a
software reader, and `Review` carries the role-noun //reviewer// — the one name in either candidate set that
leans toward the identity it must not become. Both stood flagged when the roster was ruled.
They stand because the alternates each cost more: every substitute for `Source` was either
finance-owned or a novel vehicle, and every substitute for `Review` was owned by one function outright. ''The
strain is recorded so a later reader meets a ruling rather than a fault.''

⚠ ''NO `pull/` VALUE MAY SHARE A WORD WITH A LOOP PHASE.'' Draft moved from `act` to `design` on
operator ruling. The section already states that roster and loop correspond at no point; a single shared token
would let a reader build the bijection out of one coincidence, and one coincidence is all a false pattern
needs. ''The rows now read `repair · open-close · expand · design · close` against
`observe · orient · decide · act · aftermath`, and no token appears in both.'' The prose disclaimer and the
vocabulary now enforce the same rule, which is what a pattern integrity looks like when it stops depending on
a reader having read the sentence.

⚠ ''THE GUARDS RE-CUT TO BEAT GRAIN, BECAUSE THE TWIN LICENSES MID-SPAN FIRING AND THE ELDER DOES NOT.''
A guard written for a whole-turn Persona goes dark for exactly the firings the twin advertises. Audited at one
move / one sentence, three of the original five leaked: `scope-creep` needs a span to creep across,
`flatness` needs a SET of options before one can read flat, and `sealed-close` and `broken-panel` both name
TURN-POSITION faults a Persona firing in paragraph two has no close and no panel to break. They stand re-cut
to `assumed-and-silent-fork`, `pleasing-and-false-alternative` and `verdict-without-a-joint`; `priority-fog`
left Make entirely, since Make's real in-span hazard is the thing its own aside already declines.
''The general law: a guard MUST bite at the grain its Persona fires at.'' The Band
ladder already names Beat as the grain one move occupies, so the twin states the rule against its own scale
rather than against a new one.

⚠ ''INTRINSIC SELF-CORRECTION FAILS, AND `yield/checkable-clue` IS THE CURE THAT WAS ALREADY WRITTEN.''
Self-correction without external feedback does not improve reasoning and at times
degrades it; reported gains vanished once oracle labels were withdrawn (arXiv 2310.01798). A Check firing two
sentences after the Make it follows IS intrinsic self-correction — same pass, same context, no outside signal.
So the twin now states what the yield always bought: ''a same-pass Check sends its verification OUTWARD'',
handing the operator a clue to take to contact rather than rendering a verdict on the artifact it just watched
get built. The verification leaves the causal island; the Check never adjudicates inside it.

⚠ ''A NAME READS AS A TRANSITION OR AS A HEADING, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS MEASURABLE.'' Hyland's interactive
metadiscourse taxonomy splits them exactly: a TRANSITION marker carries a semantic relation between main
clauses; a FRAME marker signals discourse acts, sequences and text stages. Das & Taboada (Discourse Processes
55(8), 2018) find 92.74% of relations signalled over the RST-DT, only 10.65% by discourse markers alone and
74.54% by non-DM cues — so a Persona name sits legitimately in the majority signal class, and the GRAPHICAL
realization is the one that reads as segmentation.
''The condition that carries the most and looks like the least: irregular intervals.''
A name arriving on a schedule has become a frame marker whatever its content, because regularity IS staging
information. So the twin rules the mark rides inline, on the clause it opens, and fires where the pull changes
— never on its own line above a block.

⚠ ''THE ONE ROW FLAGGED ON THREE INSTRUMENTS.'' Widen fails to fit the pattern the other four make. The
`relation/` values `Evidence · Preparation · Enablement · Evaluation` are all four PRESENTATIONAL relations in
RST — the class that works by increasing an inclination in the reader — and `Contrast` stands multinuclear,
outside that class. Widen also collides with Frame in-span: both fire before any artifact exists, both open
rather than close, and Frame's `fork` emitted surface text near-identical to Widen's `oppose`. And Widen is
the seat that resisted naming in every register tried.
''The cure re-cuts the moves rather than the name.'' `oppose` left Widen for Check —
an adversarial reading belongs where the guard against self-grading already stands, and it gives Check a move
that fires before an artifact exists. Widen stands purely generative at `associate-invert-import-borrow`;
Frame keeps `fork`, which splits the SAME question rather than proposing a rival one.

⚠ ''THE PRIOR ART'S OWN FAILURE RULES OUT NAMING AS THE CURE.'' De Bono seated the Six Hats on colours
deliberately — "the roles are designed to be blatantly artificial, a feature which helps the student separate
their individual ego from the activity" — and the method still collapses into identity in the field:
''"people are naturally prone to make personality associations (e.g., 'David is a black thinker')".''
''The most artificial label available does not buy non-enactment.'' What the twin
holds that Six Hats lacks is the EXPIRY: a hat gets assigned per person per meeting, where a call expires with
the span it leads. ''The expiry carries the anti-collapse load, and the naming never did.'' The drift finding
seats the same conclusion — the paper measuring persona decay across eight rounds retitled to
''Instruction (In)Stability'' (arXiv 2402.10962), because the decay hits ANY standing instruction. A persona
is only the case that shows it most legibly.

⚠ ''THE NAMES MUST BE CONVENTIONAL VEHICLES, AND THIS IS A COMPREHENSION LAW RATHER THAN A TASTE ONE.''
Bowdle & Gentner (Psych Review 112(1)) find novel metaphors processed as COMPARISON —
slow structural alignment — and conventionalized ones as CATEGORIZATION, fast and direct, with conventionality
residing SOLELY IN THE VEHICLE. A novel vehicle charges every reader an alignment cost on every encounter,
which is the same cost Six Hats pays for six arbitrary colour bindings that store nothing about their modes.
''So "reads cold without a glossary" states a mechanism, never a preference'', and it disqualifies any vehicle
a reader must first align: a name must already be conventional in workplace usage for the thing it names.
A name must additionally decline to denote an ANIMATE AGENT — the Assistant-Axis work reports that steering a
model off the default-assistant region increases its tendency to identify as other entities and induces a
theatrical register (arXiv 2601.10387) — and decline any figurative or idiomatic form, the identified
exclusion class for non-native readers in the inclusive-language and BELF literature.
That last pair of constraints is the one bridge nobody has measured at this scale:
the Axis findings concern CHARACTER prompts, and a pet-name for a move-set is a far smaller object.

⚠ ''THE DECLARATION STILL DIFFS LINE AGAINST LINE.'' `Persona(Name Params)` and `Named-Persona(Type Params)`
both keep their payload, one-line body and slot in both seeds. ''`Named-Persona` keeps `Type` and inverts in
neither seed'', because its rows name genuine kinds — Default, Earned, Masked — where `Persona`'s rows name
something a reader addresses. The twin adds `call(name on)` beside them, which
the elder has no counterpart for and needs none — the sharktooth namespace already marks an invocation where
the plain dialect must spell one. `Named-Persona` carries two of the elder's three rows and drops `Masked`
under the second ruled asymmetry.

''THE CORRESPONDENCE STAYS CHECKABLE.'' Seventeen positions carrying straight across in one order, two
ruled drops, one ruled cardinality divergence at position 11, and no divergence of ORDER anywhere. A section added to either twin without its counterpart, or dropped from
one without a ruling, reads as a divergence the shared-meaning rule must then resolve. ''Counting them
exists for exactly that.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-audience>>

!! The audience, and the two contexts a mark gets read in

''THE NEAR-TERM READER RUNS CLAUDE'' — at a terminal, and in a browser. Both surfaces take the
phrasebook as a whole file the operator attaches, so the design answers to those two and to nothing
else yet. Ceilings, panels and per-event budgets wait until a surface actually refuses something.

⚠ ''AND THOSE TWO SURFACES READ A MARK OPPOSITE WAYS.'' This governs more than it first appears:

|! context |! what happens to `<<confidence 15/20>>` |! what the declarations do |
| a wiki renders it | the procedure runs, or — undeclared — it renders as ''nothing'' | ''machinery'': they make the mark appear at all |
| a transcript carries it | ''no renderer stands between'' — the characters appear as written | ''legend'': they teach the shape to a reader |

''The vanishing rule (#/the-vanishing-rule) governs the rendered context alone.''
In a chat transcript the marks survive precisely BECAUSE nothing renders them — the failure the base
grammar warns about cannot occur where no renderer stands. So the phrasebook meets its two audiences
through one property read two ways, and neither reading needs a second artifact.

''WHICH REDEEMS THE DECLARATIONS.'' A declaration reads as noise only where a reader takes it for
machinery. `\procedure persona(name params) <<name>> <<params>>` states the mark's whole shape on one line — so
what makes a mark RENDER in a wiki also TEACHES it in a transcript. One artifact, two readings, in the
house's usual manner.

''AND THE BODY CARRIES NO DECORATION IT CANNOT SPEND.'' A plain-dialect body renders its own text
verbatim, so every bracket a declaration wraps around its output rides into the transcript too. The
bodies stay bare: what the procedure says, and nothing framing it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/open-joints>>

!! Open joints ~ what waits on the operator

''THREE JOINTS CLOSED BY USE, and the phrasebook carries each:''

# ''THE CALL FORM.'' Parentheses ride the `\procedure` DECLARATION and never the call site. All three
  lawful spellings stand and all three ride: `<<hello>>` bare, defaults inside the declaration ·
  `<<hello "operator">>` positional · `<<hello who="operator">>` named. The Hello-World primer shows the
  three together, which teaches the whole call grammar in one block.
# ''THE ASIDE MARKER.'' `~` carries an inline aside inside a plain call (`… ~ propositional support`).
  The tilde means nothing to the host inside an argument, so the house's prose idiom crosses the dialect
  boundary intact.
# ''THE DECLARATION'S SEAT.'' Syntax gets taught ONCE, at first teach, beside the Hello-World primer in
  both seeds. Each remaining declaration then rides in the section that calls it. A reader meets the
  grammar before the vocabulary, and meets each mark beside the work it does.

''WHAT STILL WAITS:''

# ''NO SEED HAS RENDERED.'' Every claim about what a mark does in a wiki rests on the base grammar as
  stated, never as observed. The vanishing rule (#/the-vanishing-rule) decides this design and stands
  measured nowhere.
# ''NO STRANGER HAS READ THE TWIN.'' Position 14 rests on a premise about what a reader does with an
  empty section, and only a reader settles it.
# ''JOINT ENACTMENT HAS NOT RUN.'' Until both seeds get promoted in ONE act (#/joint-enactment), the
  younger stands where its framing puts it rather than where this design does.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-to-measure>>

!! What the house counts

```
\procedure ~Gauge(Type:"" Params:"") ~Gauge <<Type>> holds [{{{ [<Params>] }}}]
```

<<~Gauge Vanishing "counts/plain-calls-with-no-inline-declaration red/any ~ an undeclared mark renders as absence, never as text">>
<<~Gauge Verb-Test "counts/renames-failing-the-inflection-test red/any-shipped ~ the act leaves the vocabulary silently">>
<<~Gauge Divergence "counts/twin-divergences-resolved-by-preferring-the-elder red/any ~ the resolution converts the younger to a translation in practice">>
<<~Gauge Comparison "counts/how-often-the-twins-get-read-against-each-other red/near-zero ~ a stated parity nobody exercises reads as parity nobody holds">>
<<~Gauge Register-Loss "counts/fallbacks-from-plain-to-house-register red/any-unlogged ~ register loss fails OPEN and silent unless instrumented">>
<<~Gauge Correspondence "counts/section-divergences-beyond-the-two-ruled red/any ~ a count law nothing counts decays into whatever the last hand left">>
<<~Gauge Dialect "counts/sharktooth-calls-or-declarations-inside-the-plain-seed red/any ~ one character decides the dialect, so one character breaks it">>

''The fourth gauge names the failure the others cannot see.'' A doctrine of
equal force does not produce the practice of comparison — a neighbouring field states parity across
versions and exercises it in a small single-digit fraction of cases. Parity that nobody runs decays
into a preferred text and a companion, by habit rather than by ruling.

<<~/ahu>>

